---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import RelatedPages from "../components/RelatedPages.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const path = "/terms-and-conditions";
const crumbs = [{ label: "Terms & conditions", href: path }];
const updated = "September 4, 2026";
const contactEmail = "support@editpdfmetadata.com";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — EditPdfMetaData"
  description="The terms that govern your use of EditPdfMetaData: free browser-only tools, no accounts, no uploads, no warranties, and a liability limit that matches the price."
  path={path}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  keywords="terms and conditions, pdf metadata editor terms, terms of use, pdf metadata"
>
  <Nav />
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

  <main id="main">
    <div class="container-page py-16 sm:py-24">
      <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="mt-2 text-display-lg text-ink">Terms and conditions</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-mute">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <div class="mt-10 space-y-10">
          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">The short version</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              These are the terms under which we make EditPdfMetaData available. The
              tools are free, they run entirely in your web browser, and your files never
              leave your device. There is nothing to sign up for, nothing to pay, and no
              relationship beyond you using the pages on this site. By using the tools,
              you agree to the terms below.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">What we provide</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              EditPdfMetaData is a set of browser-based tools for viewing, editing,
              and removing the metadata inside PDF files. Each tool is a static web page
              with JavaScript: when you open a document, it is read into your browser's
              memory with the standard File API, processed locally, and handed back to
              you as a download.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              You may use the tools for any lawful purpose, in personal or commercial
              settings, without restriction on the number of documents you process. No
              account, payment, or personal information is required.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Your files are never uploaded</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              There is no upload endpoint on this site and no server component that could
              receive your documents. Nothing you open in the tools is transmitted,
              stored, or seen by us. The <a href="/privacy" class="text-link underline decoration-link/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-link">privacy policy</a>
              describes the small amount of data that does travel — standard request
              logs from hosting — which relates to page loads only, never to your files.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Your responsibilities</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              You are responsible for the documents you choose to process and for checking
              the results. Verify each downloaded file before you distribute, publish, or
              archive it — particularly when you have used the removal tool, which deletes
              all metadata in one action and cannot be undone.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              You agree not to use the tools to infringe the rights of others, violate
              applicable law, or attempt to disrupt or reverse-engineer the site. You
              retain all rights in the documents you process; we make no claim to them.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">No warranty</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              The tools are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any
              kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose and
              non-infringement. We do not warrant that the tools will always be available,
              that every document will be processed correctly, or that metadata removal
              or editing will satisfy any particular legal, regulatory, or professional
              requirement.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              Metadata removal cleans the metadata layer of a file. It is not a guarantee
              that a document is anonymous — embedded images, signatures, and content on
              the page itself can still identify its origin. It remains your responsibility
              to review the document and the results.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              The tools are free. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not
              liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special
              damages — including loss of data, loss of profits, or interruption of
              business — arising from your use of, or inability to use, this site or its
              tools. Because nothing is paid, nothing is owed.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Changes to the service and these terms</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-body-md text-body">
              We may add, change, or remove tools and features, and we may update these
              terms to reflect those changes. The "last updated" date above changes with
              every revision. Continued use of the site after an update means you accept
              the revised terms; material changes will be prominent enough that you can
              hardly miss them.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-14 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-surface-2/50 p-6">
          <p class="text-body-md font-medium text-ink">Questions about these terms?</p>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-body-sm text-body">
            Write to us at{" "}
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-link underline decoration-link/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-link">
              {contactEmail}
            </a>
            . For anything about how your files are handled, the{" "}
            <a href="/privacy" class="text-link underline decoration-link/30 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-link">privacy policy</a>{" "}
            answers it first.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <RelatedPages exclude={[path]} title="Read next" />
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
